 ProcessReadmes registryPath;ids;id;path;indexStamp;pause;qdmx
⍝ Walks the Registry once and fetches every README that is due; see `ReadmeIsDue`.
⍝ This is what `OnHouseKeeping` starts as a thread, so it may run for a long time without
⍝ holding anything up: with a pause between fetches a Registry of a few thousand packages
⍝ takes the best part of an hour, and nothing waits for it.
⍝ The `:Trap 0` is deliberate and is the only one in this feature. Everything it calls traps
⍝ narrowly - a missing file, a corrupt record, a connection that failed - and lets anything
⍝ else through, so what arrives here is a fault in the code rather than a fact about the
⍝ world. Two reasons it is caught all the same:
⍝ * an untrapped error would suspend the thread rather than end it, and a suspended thread
⍝   keeps its number in ⎕TNUMS for ever - which is what `OnHouseKeeping` reads to decide
⍝   whether one of these is already running. The walk would never start again.
⍝ * ∆README_TID has to be cleared whatever happens, for the same reason.
⍝ It is logged with the package it died on, and nothing is swallowed: the walk stops there,
⍝ so the same fault is met and logged again on the next run rather than being walked past.
⍝ That is on purpose. A bug here should be a nuisance until it is fixed.
 pause←1                                            ⍝ Seconds between fetches: a courtesy to GitHub
 id←'(none yet)'
 :Trap 0
     indexStamp←GetIndexStamp registryPath          ⍝ Read before the walk, recorded after it
     :For id :In ids←GetNewestPerMajor registryPath
         :If ∆SHUTDOWN≠0                            ⍝ The server is going down; stop bothering GitHub
             :Leave
         :EndIf
         path←registryPath,'/',id
         :If ReadmeIsDue path
             {}FetchAndStoreReadme path
             ⎕DL pause
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
     :If ∆SHUTDOWN=0
         RecordReadmeSweep registryPath indexStamp  ⍝ Only a walk that ran to the end counts
     :EndIf
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     LogError'Fetching READMEs stopped at "',id,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
 :EndTrap
 ∆README_TID←¯1
⍝Done
